eath  that role ended up going to Bruce Dern  and speaking of durin he once appeared  on Lancer the real series that is  featured heavily in the film Tarantino  likes to cast the same people over and  over again in a bounty law scene you'll  notice a quick cameo from actor Michael  Madsen Madsen has popped up in many of  Tarantino's movies perhaps most famously  as mr. blonde and Reservoir Dogs another  Tarantino regular Tim Roth was supposed  to play JC brings Butler his scene was  cut but his name remains in the credits  while Tarantino alums Bruce Willis and  uma Thurman aren't in the movie their  daughters Rumer Willis and Maya Hawke  each play a small role Kurt Russell  plays a stunt coordinator named Randy he  also portrayed stuntman Mike a stunt  driver turned killer in 2007's death  Proof stuntwoman zoë bell pops up to  fire cliff Boothe after he beats up  Bruce Lee fail also starred in death  Proof in addition she was Thurman stunt  double in the Kill Bill movies and a  stunt double for both Diane Kruger and  Melanie Lauren in Inglourious Basterds  speaking of Bruce Lee his influences  popped up in Tarantino's work before in  Kill Bill Vol 1 The Green Hornet theme  plays during a sequence in which the  bride played by Thurman arrives in Tokyo  and once upon a time in Hollywood  cliff refers to Leah's Cato the name of  his character in Green Hornet Lea was  associated with Roman Polanski and  Sharon Tate in real life and he even  gave each of them martial arts lessons  while the film centers around the Manson  family murders the notorious cult leader  shows up only briefly in the movie Damon  Harriman who plays Charles Manson will  also play Manson in the upcoming second  season of the Netflix series mind Hunter  Manson arrives at Tate's home in a  Twinkie truck which he reportedly drove  in real life as well in the first scene  we see of Manson's family their dumpster  diving outside a grocery store you can  hear them singing a song called I'll  never say n